You take the rucksack off your back, and slowly sink on the ground, right on the soft underlayer of herbs. You can hardly keep your eyes open,  mind clouds...
"Hey, Henry, what is wrong with you?" you hear worried voice of Conan.
"Nothing ...eh...Conan, let's rest a little. Maybe take a nap?"
"What are you talking about?! Listen, you're so pale! Henry!.."
Everything is swimming before your eyes. Like from aside you see Conan, pulling your arm, trying to pick up Doyle, lying next to you. Then comes deep oblivion.
When you come to consciousness, you find yourself in the shade with no sick fragrance to be scented. You slowly open your eyes. It looks this is the very underbrush you wanted to reach. You sit, leaning your back against the tree; still unconscious Doyle is not far. Conan is sitting near, intently watching at you.
"I thought you'd never..." he exhaled with relief.
"What happened to me?"
"It looks like those damn plants. Even I got a headache, pulling you two out of there. You just became weak in the knees and fell with no response."
"Thanks buddy..."
You hardly stand up. After awhile, Doyle opens his eyes with a low groan. 